// src/v2/lens/medium_structure_containment.dag
// Scope: medium-structure containment guard — the MediumStructureLeak GENERALIZATION of
//   v2.lens.realization_vocabulary_containment's RealizationVocabularyLeak (DESIGN §5;
//   docs/plans/emission-ingestion-inverse.md §5.1; placed on the §2 expressibility frontier
//   per docs/plans/expressibility-frontier.md). The §5 guard catches a module *importing* a
//   target AST it shouldn't; this catches the sin one rung earlier — a medium whose structure
//   has leaked out of a `Node` into a raw string. The single rule (§5.1):
//
//     A target medium — and every sub-language embedded in it — stays a modeled `Node` from
//     authoring through checking. A raw string is legitimate ONLY at the realization edge
//     (the grammar-row emitter). BOTH writing target syntax as a string literal AND
//     inspecting emitted output with string ops are the same leak.
//
//   Two faces of one leak (DESIGN §2-horizontal — one concept, two breadths):
//     (a) emit-side    — a string LITERAL containing a grounded medium syntax marker (the GHA
//                        expression delimiter `${{`) authored OUTSIDE the realization edge.
//                        This reads AUTHORING source for a grounded token — NOT a re-ingest of
//                        emitted output: emitted output is SUPPOSED to carry target syntax, so
//                        flagging it there would wall the realization edge this guard protects.
//     (b1) check-side  — a string-op (`string_contains`/`starts_with`/…) whose RECEIVER traces
//                        (≤1 intra-fn `let` hop) to a CALL of a grounded emit fn. A
//                        `string_contains(expected_ci_yml(), "${{ env.X }}")` check is an ad-hoc
//                        partial RE-INGEST (§4: emission = ingestion⁻¹) — fragile, lossy,
//                        fail-open. The receiver is identified as an emitted-medium value by
//                        call-target PROVENANCE, NEVER by guessing from the string's contents —
//                        else the DETECTOR becomes the heuristic it forbids. (The heavier `(b2)`
//                        — receiver whose declared TYPE is `Medium<R>` — needs resolver type
//                        info and is a NAMED follow-on, see roster note; not built here.)
//
// MECHANISM (N+M — NOT a new lens mechanism): a SIBLING of the §5 LayerImportFact sweep over a
//   NEW host-enumerated candidate-fact stream. The host (medium_structure_project.rs) does the
//   mechanical Node walk — marker-in-literal for (a), emit-fn-receiver for (b1) — taking the
//   grounded policy below as parameters. This module owns ALL policy (markers, emit-fn roster,
//   string-op set, realization-edge allowset, exception roster) and applies the edge+roster
//   predicate; the host emits candidates, the lens filters (exactly as layering does).
//
// GROUNDING (§3): the per-medium marker set is the REAL upstream token, cited from the medium's
//   spec, never an invented heuristic. v1 populates GHA-expr (`${{`, the GitHub Actions
//   expression delimiter). CI-YAML-structure and shell-in-`run:` are NAMED rows with EMPTY
//   marker sets: their structural tokens (YAML `:`/`-`/`|`, shell metacharacters) are
//   ubiquitous, so a token-grep would BE the heuristic the rule forbids — a sound grounded set
//   needs the medium modeled as a `Node` (the ① fix), so their ② is intentionally deferred.
//
// RATCHET — honest, fail-closed, SHRINKING (DESIGN §5; ② now → ① wall). The current leakers go
//   RED under a pure wall, so they ride a FROZEN exception roster that only shrinks (NOT a
//   live-grep, which would be vacuous — DESIGN §5/§6 coverage-by-illusion). A new (unrostered)
//   non-edge leaker goes RED immediately.
//   dissolve-on (per medium): the medium becomes a `Medium<R>` `Node` emitted via grammar rows,
//     at which point a check is a model WALK or UNWRITABLE and the leak dissolves. For GHA-expr
//     this is witty-wolf-587's extdeps.github.expressions (serialize_expression + interpolate):
//     the GHA roster entries empty when (a) extdeps.github.expressions exists AND (b) ci_workflow
//     + the runner-env witness consume serialize_expression with ZERO inline `${{ }}` strings and
//     ZERO string-grep over emitted YAML (tracked on PR #5499; emit-side half already met there).
//
// Consumer (executable, §5): the live witnesses under
//   src/v2/test/claim/medium_structure_containment/ — floor-auto-discovered `test fn`s that scan
//   the real tree by execution (clean-tree GREEN + planted-leak RED receipt), plus the
//   hardcoded-fact lens-unit discriminators.

module v2.lens.medium_structure_containment
import v2.lens.common.construction_justification { ConstructionJustification, WallAfterGrounding }

import v2.std.algebra {
  fold_list,
  is_empty,
  is_prefix_of,
  length,
  list_append,
  list_snoc_item
}
import v2.std.collection { List }
import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import v2.std.text { Char, String }

// ── fact / violation types ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Which face of the leak (DESIGN §2-horizontal).
type MediumLeakFace
  = InlineSyntaxLiteral
  | EmittedMediumStringOp

// One host-projected candidate fact (medium_structure_leak_facts): a marker-in-literal hit
// (emit-side) or a string-op over an emitted-medium receiver (check-side). `detail` carries the
// grounded evidence — the marker for emit-side, "op@emit_fn" for check-side — so the medium is
// recoverable (§5.1 census) without minting a parallel medium enum.
type MediumStructureLeakFact {
  path: String
  face: MediumLeakFace
  detail: String
}

// One violation row (the lens output).
type MediumStructureLeak {
  path: String
  face: MediumLeakFace
  detail: String
}

data empty_medium_structure_leaks: List<MediumStructureLeak> = []

data empty_medium_marker_list: List<String> = []

// ── single-authority policy: grounded per-medium syntax markers (emit-side) ──────

// One medium's grounded syntax-marker set. Media are ROWS (§2-horizontal): a new medium is a
// row here, never a new lens.
type MediumMarkers {
  medium: String
  markers: List<String>
}

data medium_syntax_markers: List<MediumMarkers> = [
  // GitHub Actions expression language: the expression delimiter `${{ <expr> }}`, cited from
  // GitHub Actions "Evaluate expressions in workflows and actions". The opening delimiter `${{`
  // is the grounded structural token (its presence in a string literal is the medium leaking
  // out of a `Node`). Dissolve-on: witty-wolf-587's extdeps.github.expressions.
  MediumMarkers { medium: "GitHubActionsExpression", markers: ["${{"] },
  // CI YAML structure: DEFERRED (empty) — YAML structural tokens (":", "-", "|") are ubiquitous,
  // so a token-grep would be the heuristic the rule forbids. Grounded detection needs YAML
  // modeled as a `Node` (the ① fix). Named row, populated when that lands.
  MediumMarkers { medium: "CiYamlStructure", markers: [] },
  // shell-in-`run:`: DEFERRED (empty) — shell metacharacters are ubiquitous; same reasoning.
  // (The bash AST's *imported-sidecar* face is already walled by the §5 realization-vocab guard.)
  MediumMarkers { medium: "ShellInRun", markers: [] }
]

// ── single-authority policy: grounded emit-fn roster (check-side, the (b1) provenance set) ──

// The grounded emit fns: each returns an EMITTED MEDIUM (a serialized target string / Medium<R>)
// — a serializer (byte authority) or a target-script builder. A string-op whose receiver is a
// call to one of these is inspecting emitted output by string (§5.1 check-side). This hand-list
// is itself ② residue; it dissolves under the (b2) follow-on (receiver declared-type Medium<R>,
// via resolver structural reflection), which makes the provenance a type read, not a name list.
data emitted_medium_emit_fns: List<String> = [
  "expected_ci_yml",            // gunbc.ci_yaml_emit — the emitted CI workflow YAML
  "ci_yml_drifted",             // gunbc.ci_yaml_emit — a drifted CI YAML variant
  "serialize_yaml",             // extdeps.formats.yaml — YAML byte authority
  "serialize_bash",             // extdeps.languages.bash.program — bash byte authority
  "serialize_expression",       // extdeps.github.expressions — GHA-expr byte authority (witty-wolf-587)
  "interpolate",                // extdeps.github.expressions — the `${{ }}` delimiter wrapper
  "serialize_template",         // extdeps.github.expressions — GHA expression-template authority
  "gunbc_ci_workflow_run",      // a CI workflow shell-script builder
  "gunbc_ci_run_script",        // a CI run shell-script builder
  "scheduler_invoke",           // the CI scheduler-invocation shell fragment
  "git_fetch_script",           // a git-fetch shell-script builder
  "ci_release_build_script",    // a release-build shell-script builder
  "witness_layer_source_flags"  // the source-root shell flags fragment
]

// The grounded content-inspecting string ops (std/text). `string_length` is NOT here — it reads
// size, not structure, so it is not a re-ingest.
data emitted_medium_string_ops: List<String> = [
  "string_contains",
  "starts_with",
  "ends_with",
  "substring",
  "char_at"
]

// ── realization edge + scan roots ────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Realization-edge path PREFIXES — the only places a medium's raw syntax is legitimate: the
// medium models / byte authorities (where serialize_* PRODUCES the target syntax), the language
// models, and the emit fold. A `${{` literal or an emitted-medium string-op here is the edge
// doing its job, not a leak.
data medium_realization_edge_path_prefixes: List<String> = [
  "dsl/extdeps/github/",
  "src/v2/extdeps/github/",
  "dsl/extdeps/communication/medium.dag",
  "dsl/extdeps/languages/",
  "src/v2/extdeps/languages/",
  "src/v2/compiler/05_emit",
  "src/v2/compiler/06_translate",
  "src/v2/compiler/self_host/candidate_generation",
  // This guard's OWN module: it MUST name the grounded marker (`${{`) as a string literal to
  // detect it — that single-authority token definition is the detection vocabulary, definitionally
  // exempt (exactly as the §5 realization-vocab guard names the forbidden module in its own vocab).
  "src/v2/lens/medium_structure_containment.dag"
]

// Emit-side scan roots — consumer AUTHORING source, EXCLUDING test trees (a planted fixture
// carries target syntax by design; it is scanned in isolation by the RED receipt). Same roots
// as the §5 guard's consumer scan.
data medium_emit_side_scan_roots: List<String> = [
  "dsl/std",
  "dsl/extdeps",
  "dsl/compiler",
  "dsl/tools",
  "dsl/gunbc",
  "src/v2/std",
  "src/v2/extdeps",
  "src/v2/compiler",
  "src/v2/workflow",
  "src/v2/lens"
]

// Check-side scan roots — the consumer roots PLUS the test trees. UNLIKE the §5 guard (which
// excludes tests), the check-side leak LIVES in the witnesses (the _test.dag files that grep
// emitted medium output), so the scan MUST include test trees or it cannot see the thing it
// exists to catch. The precision that keeps this from being noisy is the receiver-PROVENANCE
// gate (only emitted-medium receivers), NOT excluding tests — a test doing string_contains on a
// non-medium string is fine.
// NOTE the test roots are scoped to `*/test/claim` (the witness/claim trees), NOT the whole
// `*/test`: that includes the witnesses where the check-side leak lives while EXCLUDING
// `*/test/fixture/**`, where the planted-leak RED receipt's fixture carries target syntax by
// design (it is scanned in isolation by that receipt, never here).
data medium_check_side_scan_roots: List<String> = [
  "dsl/std",
  "dsl/extdeps",
  "dsl/compiler",
  "dsl/tools",
  "dsl/gunbc",
  "dsl/test/claim",
  "src/v2/std",
  "src/v2/extdeps",
  "src/v2/compiler",
  "src/v2/workflow",
  "src/v2/lens",
  "src/v2/test/claim"
]

// SHRINKING exception roster — the leakers that exist TODAY, frozen so a NEW unrostered leaker
// goes RED. Each empties when its medium is modeled as a `Node` (the dissolve-on above). DO NOT
// ADD ROWS for code authored after this guard — a new non-edge leaker is a MediumStructureLeak
// and must model the medium, not be rostered. Reconciled by execution against the live tree at
// merge time (the clean-tree witness must report ZERO over this roster).
data medium_structure_exception_roster: List<String> = [
  // emit-side (inline `${{` in a string literal):
  "dsl/gunbc/ci_workflow.dag",          // 5 GHA expression sites — witty-wolf-587 #5499 migrates them
  "dsl/extdeps/formats/yaml.dag",       // YAML serializer sniffs `${{` for a quoting decision (nested-medium leak)
  // check-side (string-op over an emitted-medium value):
  "dsl/test/claim/ci_yaml_serializer_witness_test.dag",  // ~30 greps over expected_ci_yml() / serialize_yaml()
  "dsl/test/claim/ci_runner_seam_witness_test.dag",      // greps emitted YAML for the runner line
  "src/v2/test/claim/ci_spec_witness_test.dag"           // greps emitted CI shell scripts
]

// ── predicate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

fn char_eq(a: Char, b: Char) -> Bool {
  a == b
}

fn list_contains_str(xs: List<String>, target: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(
    xs: xs,
    empty: false,
    cons: fn(acc, s) { acc || (s == target) }
  )
}

fn path_has_any_prefix(prefixes: List<String>, path: String) -> Bool {
  fold_list(
    xs: prefixes,
    empty: false,
    cons: fn(acc, p) { acc || is_prefix_of(prefix: p, xs: path, eq: char_eq) }
  )
}

fn path_is_medium_realization_edge(path: String) -> Bool {
  path_has_any_prefix(prefixes: medium_realization_edge_path_prefixes, path: path)
}

// Flatten the per-medium marker table to the flat list the host scans for (single authority —
// the table feeds both the host and the census mapping; no second representation).
// A typed projector — calling it with the fold element pins the element type (a bare `m.markers`
// field access cannot, as the inferencer needs the type to look the field up).
fn marker_set(m: MediumMarkers) -> List<String> {
  m.markers
}

fn flatten_marker_rows(rows: List<MediumMarkers>) -> List<String> {
  fold_list(
    xs: rows,
    empty: empty_medium_marker_list,
    cons: fn(acc, m) { list_append(left: acc, right: marker_set(m: m)) }
  )
}

fn all_medium_markers() -> List<String> {
  flatten_marker_rows(rows: medium_syntax_markers)
}

// A leak: a host-projected candidate whose path is NEITHER a realization-edge module NOR carried
// by the (shrinking) exception roster. The host already established the candidate (marker present
// / emitted-medium receiver); this is the edge+roster filter. Roster is an explicit parameter so
// a witness can prove the ratchet shrinks honestly (drop a member → its live leak goes RED).
fn is_medium_structure_leak(fact: MediumStructureLeakFact, roster: List<String>) -> Bool {
  (path_is_medium_realization_edge(path: fact.path) == false)
    && (list_contains_str(xs: roster, target: fact.path) == false)
}

// ── scan / count / holds ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

fn scan_facts_for_medium_leaks(
  facts: List<MediumStructureLeakFact>,
  roster: List<String>
) -> List<MediumStructureLeak> {
  fold_list(
    xs: facts,
    empty: empty_medium_structure_leaks,
    cons: fn(acc, fact) {
      if is_medium_structure_leak(fact: fact, roster: roster) {
        list_snoc_item(
          xs: acc,
          item: MediumStructureLeak {
            path: fact.path,
            face: fact.face,
            detail: fact.detail
          }
        )
      } else {
        acc
      }
    }
  )
}

fn medium_structure_leak_count(
  facts: List<MediumStructureLeakFact>,
  roster: List<String>
) -> Int {
  length(xs: scan_facts_for_medium_leaks(facts: facts, roster: roster))
}

fn medium_structure_containment_holds(
  facts: List<MediumStructureLeakFact>,
  roster: List<String>
) -> Bool {
  is_empty(xs: scan_facts_for_medium_leaks(facts: facts, roster: roster))
}

// ── canonical-roster convenience (binds the single-authority roster) ──────────────

fn medium_structure_leak_count_canonical(facts: List<MediumStructureLeakFact>) -> Int {
  medium_structure_leak_count(facts: facts, roster: medium_structure_exception_roster)
}

fn medium_structure_containment_holds_canonical(facts: List<MediumStructureLeakFact>) -> Bool {
  medium_structure_containment_holds(facts: facts, roster: medium_structure_exception_roster)
}

// ── live projection (the new sibling host enumerator over the real tree) ──────────

// Project candidate facts over the given roots (host Node walk), then apply the canonical-roster
// edge+roster predicate. emit_roots feed detector (a); check_roots feed detector (b1).
fn medium_structure_leak_count_live(
  emit_roots: List<String>,
  check_roots: List<String>
) -> Int {
  medium_structure_leak_count_canonical(
    facts: medium_structure_leak_facts(
      emit_roots: emit_roots,
      check_roots: check_roots,
      markers: all_medium_markers(),
      emit_fns: emitted_medium_emit_fns,
      string_ops: emitted_medium_string_ops
    )
  )
}

fn medium_structure_containment_clean_live(
  emit_roots: List<String>,
  check_roots: List<String>
) -> Bool {
  medium_structure_containment_holds_canonical(
    facts: medium_structure_leak_facts(
      emit_roots: emit_roots,
      check_roots: check_roots,
      markers: all_medium_markers(),
      emit_fns: emitted_medium_emit_fns,
      string_ops: emitted_medium_string_ops
    )
  )
}

// Construction-justification (DESIGN §5/§6, ROADMAP §0; expressibility-frontier §2). Layered ON
// TOP of the #5433 inert-lens import-closure backstop.
data construction_justification: ConstructionJustification = ConstructionJustification {
  class: WallAfterGrounding {
    grounding_authority: "each medium modeled as a Medium<R> Node emitted via grammar rows (GHA-expr: witty-wolf-587's extdeps.github.expressions / serialize_expression); the §5 realization-vocab guard is the sibling for the imported-sidecar face",
    dissolve_on: "the exception roster empties as each medium is modeled — a check becomes a model walk or unwritable, and authoring or grepping the medium's syntax as a raw string outside the realization edge is then unwritable"
  },
  rationale: "A medium's structure leaking out of a Node into a raw string — written as a grounded-marker literal (emit-side) or grepped over an emitted-medium value (check-side, by call-target provenance) outside the realization edge — is a decidable property; this class is ② (lens residue) ONLY because the media are not all modeled yet, a shrinking-roster ratchet that becomes a pure ① construction wall as each medium becomes a Medium<R> Node."
}
